<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Although my mind with Thine agrees:</l><l>My being Thou dost own,</l><l>Some parts within would still not yield</l><l>To say, “I’m Thine alone.”</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Remind me, Lord, of what love is,</l><l>How faithfulness should be.</l><l>The universe to all declares</l><l>Thou lovest faithfully.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>The heavens, spread from sky to sky,</l><l>Bespeak Thy boundless love;</l><l>Its vast dimensions, broad and high,</l><l>We’ll never fully prove.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>The vault of heav’n has billows soft;</l><l>They tell Thy care for me;</l><l>Such gentle, kind and tender love</l><l>Towards one so harsh towards Thee.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Surrounding range, majestic, sure,</l><l>Thy faithfulness displays.</l><l>Withstanding all, Thy love’s secure,</l><l>Immutable always.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>For birds aloft and trees aground,</l><l>What thorough care I see!</l><l>Thy loving care for me abounds</l><l>E’en more unceasingly.</l></lg>
<lg label="8."><l>Love vast, yet thorough; strong, yet sweet,</l><l>I praise with joyful tears;</l><l>I’ll love Thee, Lord, with all my heart</l><l>Today and all my years.</l></lg>
<lg label="9."><l>Trustworthy, changeless, faithful, true—</l><l>I fain would learn from Thee,</l><l>That with my heart, though weak, I too</l><l>Can love Thee faithfully!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
